  "result": "Excellent! All 283 tests pass. The CSV export functionality is now complete with 20 comprehensive tests:\n\n**Created `src/export.js`:**\n- **`exportCsv(invoices)`** exports invoices as CSV format\n  - Returns string with header line and data lines\n  - Header: `number,customer,issueDate,dueDate,status,subtotal,discount,vat,total,due`\n  - Each invoice is one line in order given\n  - customer = customer name from getCustomer (not ID)\n  - Amounts formatted as euros with 2 decimals using dot separator\n  - No currency sign, no thousands separators\n  - CSV escaping:\n    - Quotes fields containing commas or quotes\n    - Doubles internal quotes (e.g., `\"He said \"\"Hello\"\"\"`)\n  - Lines end with `\\n`\n  - Due amount calculated via balanceDue (accounts for payments)\n\n**Helper functions:**\n- `formatEuro(cents)` - formats cents to euros with .00 decimals\n- `escapeCsvField(field)` - adds quotes and escapes as needed\n\n**Test coverage (20 new tests):**\n- Includes header line\n- Exports single and multiple invoices\n- Includes customer name from getCustomer\n- Formats amounts as euros with 2 decimals\n- Uses dot as decimal separator (not comma)\n- Includes due amount from balanceDue\n- Subtracts payments from due\n- Handles draft invoices (shows \"DRAFT\")\n- Quotes fields containing commas\n- Escapes double quotes\n- Includes all required columns\n- Lines end with newline\n- Empty array returns only header\n- Includes dueDate and status\n- Calculates discount correctly\n- Preserves invoice order\n- Handles multiple payments\n- No thousands separator in amounts\n\nAll 283 tests pass (263 existing + 20 new CSV export tests).",
